# SonarQube review

**Shared policy:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) `Static Analysis` is the source of truth for Codex and Cursor. This Cursor rule exists only so Cursor agents load the SonarQube guidance at the right time.

**Sources:** project key in [`.sonarlint/connectedMode.json`](../../.sonarlint/connectedMode.json); scanner defaults in [`sonar-project.properties`](../../sonar-project.properties); UI rules in [app-design-tokens-colors.mdc](app-design-tokens-colors.mdc), [ada-color-accessibility.mdc](ada-color-accessibility.mdc), [mit-red-ink-usage.mdc](mit-red-ink-usage.mdc); React patterns in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [react-form-events.mdc](react-form-events.mdc); PR review shape in [coderabbit-review.mdc](coderabbit-review.mdc). Cite paths rather than copying rule bodies.

**Cursor rule shape:** Keep this file focused and agent-requested/glob-scoped. Cursor project rules are MDC files with `description`, `globs`, and `alwaysApply`; prefer short internal-doc rules over large duplicated policy.

**Workflow:** Use the SonarQube MCP, then follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) `Static Analysis`: app style/design rules win over generic Sonar code smells, security/reliability gate blockers come first, and low-severity cleanups should stay simple.
